.TH JIMAKU 1 "2026-10-28" "jimaku" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jimaku \- download subtitles for videos and save them as UTF-8
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jimaku
.br
.B jimaku
.RI [ options ] " " [ video | folder ...]
.br
.B jimaku doctor
.br
.B jimaku version
.br
.B jimaku help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jimaku
asks
.BR subliminal (1)
for a subtitle for each video it is given, and for every video at the top of
each folder it is given, then makes sure the subtitles beside those videos are
UTF-8 without a byte order mark. A subtitle in Latin-1, Windows-1252 or UTF-16
is converted, so players and TVs that only read UTF-8 show accents right.
.PP
Videos are recognized by extension: mkv, mp4, m4v, avi, mov, wmv, webm, mpg,
mpeg, ts, m2ts, flv, ogm, divx and 3gp, in any case. Hidden files and
subfolders are left alone. A file named on the command line is used whatever
its extension.
.PP
Before downloading anything, jimaku prints how many videos it found and what
it will do. Without a target on a terminal it asks for one, offering the
current folder; outside a terminal it works on the current folder. A video for
which no subtitle is found is named in a warning.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
List subliminal with its version and the text tools jimaku needs, with the
flavor and version of each. Exits non-zero when one is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version and the platform.
.TP
.B help
Print the usage page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-language " code"
The subtitle language, an IETF code such as
.BR pt\-BR ,
.B en
or
.BR es .
Default
.BR pt\-BR .
.TP
.BR \-\-force ", " \-\-no\-force
Replace a subtitle that is already there, or skip a video that already has
one. Default yes.
.TP
.BR \-\-hearing\-impaired ", " \-\-no\-hearing\-impaired
Put subtitles for the hearing impaired first, or last. Default no. With a
subliminal older than its subtitle categories, the default leaves the choice
to subliminal.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
List every video and download nothing.
.PP
Every option that takes a value also takes the form
.IR \-\-name = value ,
and
.B \-\-
ends the options. A folder named help, doctor or version is reached by giving
its path, such as
.IR ./help .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every video got a subtitle, or there was no video. 1 when a video got
no subtitle, subliminal failed, subliminal is missing, or the arguments are
wrong.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B jimaku ~/Movies
Fetch pt-BR subtitles for every video in the Movies folder.
.TP
.B jimaku \-\-language en film.mkv
Fetch an English subtitle for one video.
.TP
.B jimaku \-\-dry\-run .
List the videos in the current folder.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR subliminal (1),
.BR iconv (1),
.BR file (1)
